WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.069 --> 00:00:05.759
The stellar cast of the Hunger Games reunites
for the final time as Katniss makes a last

00:00:05.759 --> 00:00:08.780
stand against President Snow in the Mockingjay
Part 2.

00:00:08.780 --> 00:00:12.700
I'm Jan and this is 20 things you probably
didn't know about The Hunger Games: Mockingjay

00:00:12.700 --> 00:00:13.700
movies.

00:00:13.700 --> 00:00:19.230
For production designer Philip Messina, the
most complicated set to create was the Capitol's

00:00:19.230 --> 00:00:23.519
tunnels, which were about five-foot high,
making it a tough location for both cast and

00:00:23.519 --> 00:00:28.500
crew, who also had real fire and water, cold,
complex fight sequences, and 20-lbs of waterlogged

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.439
gear to deal with during those scenes.

00:00:30.439 --> 00:00:34.780
In fact, the action in those scenes was so
intricate that, before filming began, the

00:00:34.780 --> 00:00:39.120
entire thing was storyboarded and choreographed.
And filming took place over the course of

00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:41.550
three weeks on a soundstage in Atlanta.

00:00:41.550 --> 00:00:45.840
Oh, and those mutts Katniss and co do battle
with were actually brought to life thanks

00:00:45.840 --> 00:00:48.800
to a mix of stuntmen on set and CGI.

00:00:48.800 --> 00:00:53.030
The assault by lizard mutts wasn't just a
terrifying moment for the movie's characters;

00:00:53.030 --> 00:00:57.829
it also got pretty scary for actor Wes Chatham,
who plays cameraman Castor who films District

00:00:57.829 --> 00:01:02.530
13's propos with his brother Pollux and director
Cressida. While filming a scene where one

00:01:02.530 --> 00:01:06.990
of the mutts attacked his character, Chatham
nearly drowned as a stunt performer accidentally

00:01:06.990 --> 00:01:08.390
held him under water.

00:01:08.390 --> 00:01:13.130
A number of other actors also sustained injuries
during the tunnel sequence. Liam Hemsworth,

00:01:13.130 --> 00:01:17.460
who plays Gale, hurt his back after being
thrown against a wall and badly bruised his

00:01:17.460 --> 00:01:22.610
hips after rolling over steel grates for multiple
takes. While those same grates led to Josh

00:01:22.610 --> 00:01:26.759
Hutcherson, who plays Peeta, fracturing his
knee.

00:01:26.759 --> 00:01:31.140
Actor Sam Claflin loved having the chance
to wield Finnick's trident against those monstrous

00:01:31.140 --> 00:01:35.650
mutts, and before filming Part 2, he spent
time practising with broomsticks to keep up

00:01:35.650 --> 00:01:36.650
his skills!

00:01:36.650 --> 00:01:40.600
And although Claflin found Mockingjay Part
2 the most physically demanding of The Hunger

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:44.380
Games movies, he says his biggest challenge
was actually the dance scene at Finnick's

00:01:44.380 --> 00:01:49.610
wedding to Annie Cresta as he absolutely hates
dancing!

00:01:49.610 --> 00:01:54.430
The map projected by the holo Katniss and
her team use to avoid traps in the Capitol

00:01:54.430 --> 00:01:59.020
is based in part on the layout of France's
capital city, Paris, where filming for some

00:01:59.020 --> 00:02:01.270
scenes in the Mockingjay movies took place.

00:02:01.270 --> 00:02:05.630
For example, the scene where a pod releases
a deluge of black oil on Katniss and her team

00:02:05.630 --> 00:02:10.660
was filmed in Les Espaces D'Abraxas, a post-modern
apartment complex in the Parisian suburbs.

00:02:10.660 --> 00:02:14.020
And for many of the scenes set in President
Snow's mansion in the Capitol, including his

00:02:14.020 --> 00:02:18.430
office, the filmmakers used a mansion not
far from Paris called the Château de Voisins.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:22.700
Speaking of Snow's office, the rug in that
room was woven in China especially for the

00:02:22.700 --> 00:02:25.319
production and measured 45 feet.

00:02:25.319 --> 00:02:29.300
Remember the podium we saw President Snow
standing at in The Hunger Games movies? Well,

00:02:29.300 --> 00:02:33.950
the filmmakers actually destroyed that prop
after each film, only to rebuild it for the

00:02:33.950 --> 00:02:38.420
next one! Oh, and by the way, it may look
pretty sturdy on screen, but in reality it's

00:02:38.420 --> 00:02:42.650
made from cheap, lightweight materials like
plywood and Styrofoam!

00:02:42.650 --> 00:02:47.970
For the look of Katniss's Mockingjay outfit,
costume designers Kurt and Bart drew on Japanese

00:02:47.970 --> 00:02:50.900
archery gear, specifically their asymmetrical
breastplates, and the mockingjay bird itself

00:02:50.900 --> 00:02:51.900
provided inspiration for the outfit's colour.

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:54.819
Because Jennifer Lawrence wears the outfit
in a number of different scenes, its function

00:02:54.819 --> 00:02:58.739
and flexibility were as important as how it
looked. So, at the first costume fitting,

00:02:58.739 --> 00:03:03.819
she ran around with her bow and arrow so Kurt
&amp; Bart could work out where and how the outfit

00:03:03.819 --> 00:03:04.819
needed altering.

00:03:04.819 --> 00:03:08.670
For example, they built an arm guard into
the costume on Lawrence's shooting arm when

00:03:08.670 --> 00:03:12.510
they realised that the bow string was hitting
her forearm whenever she shot an arrow.

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:17.830
When creating costumes for District 13's inhabitants,
designers Kurt and Bart looked to World War

00:03:17.830 --> 00:03:22.450
Two London for ideas. They especially kept
in mind the wartime restrictions placed on

00:03:22.450 --> 00:03:27.150
the garment industry to save fabric, for example,
the number of buttons on clothes and the amount

00:03:27.150 --> 00:03:28.629
of pleats in dresses.

00:03:28.629 --> 00:03:32.549
For Effie Trinket's distinct take on District
13's clothing, costume designers Kurt and

00:03:32.549 --> 00:03:37.349
Bart were inspired by their experience of
New York's club scene in the late 1980s and

00:03:37.349 --> 00:03:42.780
the often eccentric fashion of American socialite
Edith Bouvier Beale, who was known as Little

00:03:42.780 --> 00:03:47.060
Edie and featured in the 1975 documentary
film Grey Gardens.

00:03:47.060 --> 00:03:51.190
By the way, the Mockingjay movies are not
the first time costume designers Kurt &amp; Bart

00:03:51.190 --> 00:03:55.920
have worked with director Francis Lawrence.
They also worked with him in 2001 on the music

00:03:55.920 --> 00:03:59.780
video for Brittany Spears's song "I'm A Slave
4 U".

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:04.360
After taking care of Elizabeth Banks' make-up
for the first two films in the franchise,

00:04:04.360 --> 00:04:08.310
Make-up Designer Ve Neill decided to place
Effie Trinket's appearance in the hands of

00:04:08.310 --> 00:04:13.010
her colleague Nikoletta Skarlatos to ensure
a fresh perspective and a suitably different

00:04:13.010 --> 00:04:16.190
look for the ever-changing Effie in the final
two movies.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:21.509
Transforming actress Jena Malone into Johanna
took 3 hours in the make-up chair each day,

00:04:21.509 --> 00:04:26.000
which included putting on a bald cap, doing
flesh toning and prosthetic work around her

00:04:26.000 --> 00:04:29.810
neck, and adding cuts and bruises.

00:04:29.810 --> 00:04:34.100
Jennifer Lawrence's young nephews, Bear and
Theodore Lawrence, play Katniss and Peeta's

00:04:34.100 --> 00:04:38.500
children in the epilogue scene in Mockingjay
Part 2. Bear is the child with Josh Hutcherson,

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:42.979
while Theodore, who was just nine months old
when the movie was shot, is in Jennifer Lawrence's

00:04:42.979 --> 00:04:43.979
arms.

